// A thunk is a function that takes zero arguments.
// Callbacks are often useful for precisely timing actions.
[[-> call_func]]
// Exit accepts a callback, for example. This is called right as the dialog window closes
[exit: [-> player play_anim: Goodbye]]

// Lambda functions are more complex, but allow for chaining operations using [|]
[exit: [_ -> [game set_stat: linda/endgame | #4] | [main_speaker set_latest: We're going to talk to Carly.]]]
// The also allow for arguments, which can be tricky to use due to the default syntax rules.
// Here, I've just escaped all the logic and inserted raw code
[do_something_with_function: [a b c -> #var x = a + b + c  | #x]]